.TH HOKAN 1 "2026-08-20" "hokan 0.1.0-beta.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hokan \- shell-aware terminal completion overlay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hokan
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hokan starts an interactive zsh, bash, or fish inside a PTY and renders an
inline completion list below the real shell prompt. Candidates come from shell
history, built-in command recipes, the filesystem, package.json scripts,
subcommands and flags read from man pages (HELP rows, for commands without a
built-in spec), and an explicitly selected supported AI provider.
.PP
Hokan does not use the terminal alternate screen for its overlay. AI results,
history entries, and commands classified as high or unknown risk are inserted
for review and are never executed by candidate selection.
.PP
Zsh powerline-class themes (powerlevel10k, oh-my-zsh agnoster) are supported:
prompt bytes, including Nerd Font private-use glyphs, pass through byte-exactly,
and the overlay hides and re-anchors when an unknown terminal sequence appears.
.PP
The overlay is a compact rounded-border box anchored under the cursor column:
per-command Nerd Font icons, typed-prefix highlighting, right-aligned source
tags, pagination and key hints embedded in the border edges. Set
.B nerd_fonts = false
in the [ui] section of config.toml if the terminal font lacks Nerd Font
glyphs; defaults are max_rows = 8 (six candidate rows plus two border rows)
and max_width = 76.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --shell " " zsh|bash|fish
Select the interactive child shell. The default is derived from
.BR $SHELL .
.TP
.B --login
Start the child as a login shell.
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Print help.
.TP
.BR -V , " " --version
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "init " SHELL
Print versioned shell integration code.
.TP
.B install
Install a managed integration block in the selected shell rc file. Existing
files are backed up, and repeated installs are idempotent. Use
.B --rc-file
to select an explicit file, or
.B --on-demand
to install an
.B hk
command instead of automatic startup. New interactive zsh, bash, and fish
sessions automatically start Hokan; the completion hook is loaded only in the
managed child shell. The automatic wrapper preserves the underlying shell so
.B hokan-leave
can return to it.
.TP
.B setup
Compatibility alias for
.BR install .
.TP
.B uninstall [--integration-only]
Remove managed shell integration while preserving configuration, credentials,
custom specs, history, and logs. When the release installer owns the current
binary, plain
.B uninstall
also removes that binary, its man page, and its updater backup. Package-manager
binaries remain owned by their package manager. Use
.B --integration-only
to always preserve the executable.
.TP
.B doctor [--json]
Inspect TTY, terminal, shell, configuration, directory permissions, AI, and
active shell integration state.
.TP
.BI "config " path|show|validate|init
Inspect, validate, or initialize the TOML configuration.
.TP
.B config ai
Inspect or update the OpenAI-compatible endpoint, model, and credential source.
Use
.B --api-key-stdin
to store a private credential file. This is the scripted, non-interactive path;
for an interactive provider and credential wizard use
.BR "ai setup" .
.TP
.B ai setup
Interactive guided setup for AI providers and credentials: choose account
sign-in (ChatGPT/Codex, Gemini Code Assist, or xAI Grok), a direct API
(including OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Groq, Mistral, Kimi, Z.AI, Qwen,
Hugging Face, NVIDIA NIM, NovitaAI, DeepInfra, and MiniMax), a subscription or
gateway (OpenCode, OpenRouter, Kimi Coding Plan, Alibaba Coding Plan, Ollama
Cloud, Vercel AI Gateway, or Kilo Code), local Ollama or LM Studio, or a custom
OpenAI-compatible endpoint. The selected provider and model choose Chat
Completions, Anthropic Messages, or Responses automatically.
The wizard then supplies the credential, selects a model, and runs a connection
test. Credentials are stored per provider in credentials.toml with mode 0600;
API-key input is read with terminal echo disabled, and OAuth tokens refresh
automatically before expiry. The wizard uses a colored step-by-step terminal
UI (honoring ui.color and NO_COLOR), and requires stdin and stdout to be a
terminal; it refuses to run when they are not.
.TP
.BI "upgrade " [--check] [--channel stable|beta] [--force] [--yes]
Check GitHub releases for a newer version and install it: download the
target archive, verify it against SHA256SUMS, smoke-test the binary, back
the current one up as hokan.bak, and atomically replace it. Without flags
the command asks for confirmation interactively and requires a terminal.
.B --check
only reports availability;
.B --channel
persists the release channel (stable releases, or beta pre-releases)
before upgrading. Automatic background updates use the same code path and
are controlled by the
.B [update]
config section and the HOKAN_NO_AUTO_UPDATE environment variable.
.TP
.BI "history " import|stats|prune|repair|compact|clear
Import and maintain Hokan's private history store. Clearing requires
.BR --yes
and never modifies the shell's own history.
.TP
.BI "spec " list|show|validate
Inspect the effective built-in and user command specifications.
.SH SHELL COMMANDS
.TP
.B hokan-leave
Leave the active Hokan session and continue in the underlying, unwrapped shell.
The command exists only inside a Hokan-managed child shell. In automatic mode
it resumes the shell that started Hokan; in on-demand mode it returns to the
shell that called
.BR hk .
Plain
.B exit
and Ctrl-D retain their normal shell semantics and close the current session.
.SH DEFAULT KEYS
.TP
.B Up, Down
Move the current selection. When the overlay is closed at an editable prompt,
open Hokan's history-only list without installing or replacing shell key
bindings.
.TP
.B PageUp, PageDown
Move the current selection by one page.
.TP
.B Enter
With no selection, execute the command exactly as typed: the overlay is
closed and Enter is passed through to the shell. With an explicit
selection (Up/Down), Enter executes the selected candidate instead;
candidates classified High or Unknown risk first show a confirmation
row (Enter confirms, Esc cancels). Typed input never triggers a
confirmation.
.TP
.B Tab
Insert or continue the selected candidate. Tab never executes a command.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the overlay or cancel an active AI request.
.TP
.B Ctrl-R
Toggle the history-only view.
.TP
.B Shift-Tab
Show or hide the completion list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Default child shell.
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal capability identifier. TERM=dumb is not supported.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for config.toml, credentials.toml, and user command specs.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the private history store and optional diagnostic log.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for caches.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Default API credential environment variable. The configured name may differ.
.TP
.B OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY
Primary API credential for the OpenCode Go subscription endpoint.
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
API credential for OpenRouter.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GROQ_API_KEY, MISTRAL_API_KEY, TOGETHER_API_KEY
Common direct-provider credentials detected by the AI setup wizard.
.TP
.B KIMI_API_KEY, KIMI_CODING_API_KEY, ZAI_API_KEY, GLM_API_KEY, DASHSCOPE_API_KEY
Kimi/Moonshot, Z.AI/GLM, and Alibaba/DashScope credentials detected by the
wizard.
.TP
.B OPENCODE_API_KEY, OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY, AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY
OpenCode and Vercel AI Gateway credentials. OPENCODE_API_KEY is accepted as a
compatibility alias for OpenCode Go.
.TP
.B HF_TOKEN, NVIDIA_API_KEY, OLLAMA_API_KEY
Hugging Face, NVIDIA NIM, and Ollama Cloud credentials detected by the wizard.
.TP
.B STEPFUN_API_KEY, ALIBABA_CODING_PLAN_API_KEY, KILOCODE_API_KEY
StepFun, Alibaba Coding Plan, and Kilo Code credentials detected by the wizard.
.TP
.B XIAOMI_API_KEY, TOKENHUB_API_KEY, FIREWORKS_API_KEY, MINIMAX_API_KEY
Additional hosted-provider credentials detected by the wizard.
.TP
.B NOVITA_API_KEY, DEEPINFRA_API_KEY
NovitaAI and DeepInfra credentials detected by the wizard.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color when ui.color is auto.
.TP
.B HOKAN_AUTO_START
Set to 0 to bypass managed shell auto-start for the new shell process.
.TP
.B HOKAN_BIN
Override the Hokan executable used by a managed integration block or active
child-shell hook.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hokan/config.toml
Default configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hokan/credentials.toml
Optional credential file; must be owned by the user and mode 0600 or stricter.
Version 2 format stores one entry per provider: either an API key or an OAuth
access/refresh token set with expiry.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hokan/specs/
User command specifications.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/hokan/
Private event log, snapshots, locks, and import checkpoints.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/hokan/debug.log
Optional bounded JSONL diagnostic log. Disabled by default; excludes query text,
history, working-directory paths, HTTP bodies, and environment values.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/.hokan-install.toml
Private release-installer receipt used to remove only installer-owned files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Interactive mode returns the child shell exit status, capped at 255. A
.B hokan-leave
request returns zero when Hokan was launched directly or on demand; managed
auto-start consumes its private handoff marker and resumes the underlying
shell. CLI commands return zero on success and nonzero on configuration, I/O,
validation, or runtime failure.
.SH RECOVERY
On a recoverable failure Hokan restores termios and cursor state. If a forced
termination leaves terminal input or echo broken, run
.BR "stty sane" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR fish (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR zsh (1)
